1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:05,960
Hello, Zogg here. Welcome to the sixth episode
of Earthlings 101. Today we will talk about

2
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:12,960
beauty.

3
00:00:43,030 --> 00:00:48,940
Beauty is a typical earthling concept: A subjective
quality of objects, creatures, or even geometrical

4
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:50,780
forms, or ideas.

5
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:54,679
When you ask earthlings what beauty is, they
will babble about beauty being a light in

6
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:59,489
the heart, the splendor of truth, a manifestation
of secret natural laws, the sensible image

7
00:00:59,489 --> 00:01:04,409
of the Infinite, truth's smile, eternity gazing
at itself in a mirror, or even a gift from

8
00:01:04,409 --> 00:01:10,590
an imaginary bio administrator. In other words,
they have no idea. Which is strange, as earthlings

9
00:01:10,590 --> 00:01:15,909
are more attracted by beauty than Centauri
lawyers are attracted by a mass divorce.

10
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:20,340
Earthlings are attracted to all kinds of things.
Sometimes the reasons are obvious, because

11
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:26,049
the things are useful for feeding, reproducing
and not dying. But sometimes, earthlings are

12
00:01:26,049 --> 00:01:30,770
attracted to things that have apparently no
immediate use, like flowers, music, trees

13
00:01:30,770 --> 00:01:34,909
or gems. This seemingly useless appeal is
called beauty.

14
00:01:34,909 --> 00:01:38,969
An example for a beautiful object is this
painting [the Mona Lisa]. For an alien, it's

15
00:01:38,969 --> 00:01:43,829
just a picture of a female earthling in front
of a landscape. For earthlings, it's one of

16
00:01:43,829 --> 00:01:49,299
the most beautiful objects in the world. But
what makes things like this painting so particular?

17
00:01:49,299 --> 00:01:53,390
The most obvious point of beauty is that earthlings
enjoy it - and if you have learned anything

18
00:01:53,390 --> 00:01:57,539
during this course, it's probably that whenever
earthlings enjoy something, you can be pretty

19
00:01:57,539 --> 00:02:02,049
sure that the genetic imperative is behind
it. Beauty is probably no exception.

20
00:02:02,049 --> 00:02:07,729
So, instead of philosophizing about eternity
and truth, let's look at some examples. Things

21
00:02:07,729 --> 00:02:12,430
earthlings usually consider beautiful include
flowers, fertile landscapes, attractive but

22
00:02:12,430 --> 00:02:18,530
sexually unavailable females, bird songs,
precious metals and gems, impressive buildings,

23
00:02:18,530 --> 00:02:24,310
and even interesting shapes or ideas. Why
are earthlings attracted to those things?

24
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:29,120
Let's pick an example: landscapes. Experiments
have shown that earthlings consider a landscape

25
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:33,049
beautiful if it is fertile, has bodies of
fresh hydric acid and some trees that can

26
00:02:33,049 --> 00:02:38,150
be used as firewood. Interestingly, this is
exactly the kind of landscape a bio-administrator

27
00:02:38,150 --> 00:02:43,230
would chose for a settlement on an alien planet.
Usually, a bio-administrator attracts specimen

28
00:02:43,230 --> 00:02:48,209
to a region using a "positive psychical response
field emitter", commonly known as "happybox".

29
00:02:48,209 --> 00:02:53,220
Whoever approaches the emission range of the
happybox becomes instantly happy. So, specimen

30
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:57,170
settle in these regions and start cultivating
them happily, even if their efforts will only

31
00:02:57,170 --> 00:03:02,950
bear fruits many seasons later. In other words,
a happybox is a bait, a substitute pleasure,

32
00:03:02,950 --> 00:03:05,180
a promise of future happiness.

33
00:03:05,180 --> 00:03:09,650
My guess is that beauty is exactly the same
as a happybox - only without the happybox.

34
00:03:09,650 --> 00:03:13,599
Evolution favours earthlings who settle in
landscapes where they can harvest food in

35
00:03:13,599 --> 00:03:17,640
the summer and firewood in the winter. But
earthlings usually seek immediate pleasure

36
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:22,390
rather than thinking months ahead. So, evolution
found the trick of rewarding the discovery

37
00:03:22,390 --> 00:03:27,480
of fertile landscapes immediately with a substitute
pleasure, some kind of virtual happy field,

38
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:32,209
in order to motivate them to settle there.
That's what earthlings call beauty.

39
00:03:32,209 --> 00:03:37,000
Of course, beauty is not an actual happy field.
It's a feeling generated by the Beast which

40
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:41,170
floods the ego with pleasure when seeing a
fertile landscape, or when receiving indicator

41
00:03:41,170 --> 00:03:45,129
signals for fertile landscapes such as flowers
or bird songs.

42
00:03:45,129 --> 00:03:50,819
Now, not all beautiful things are about fertile
landscapes. For many earthlings, "beauty"

43
00:03:50,819 --> 00:03:55,390
means above all "beautiful females". A female
is considered beautiful if she is sexually

44
00:03:55,390 --> 00:04:00,930
attractive but not immediately sexually available.
As I explained in episode 3, female earthlings

45
00:04:00,930 --> 00:04:05,310
are rather picky about their sexual partners
due to their limited childbearing capacity,

46
00:04:05,310 --> 00:04:10,060
so males have to make an effort to get chosen.
Now, when the female is very attractive, this

47
00:04:10,060 --> 00:04:15,019
courtship can last a while and involve many
candidates. Unfortunately, earthlings prefer

48
00:04:15,019 --> 00:04:19,860
immediate pleasure to uncertain future delight.
So, evolution needed a trick to motivate them

49
00:04:19,860 --> 00:04:25,030
not to give up too early. The trick was basically
the same as for landscapes: Beauty, a virtual

50
00:04:25,030 --> 00:04:28,090
happy field around attractive but unavailable
females.

51
00:04:28,090 --> 00:04:32,870
So, the thing that beautiful females and beautiful
landscapes have in common is simply the fact

52
00:04:32,870 --> 00:04:36,760
that they have both been tagged as "beautiful"
by evolution, as an indicator of fertility

53
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:41,640
and a promise of future happiness.
Males can also be beautiful, even more in

54
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:46,310
a society that has started questioning its
own gender roles: When males can become wooed,

55
00:04:46,310 --> 00:04:49,150
they need beauty to keep the wooers interested.

56
00:04:49,150 --> 00:04:54,460
But what about precious metals, gems and huge
buildings? Well, they are indications of another

57
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:59,580
thing that may lead to future happiness: Wealth.
When an earthling, or an earthling community,

58
00:04:59,580 --> 00:05:04,430
is wealthy, they tend to display their wealth
with rare metals, precious stones, expensive

59
00:05:04,430 --> 00:05:09,990
cloth and huge buildings. This is called,
pomp. Now, living in a wealthy city or around

60
00:05:09,990 --> 00:05:14,660
a wealthy person usually doesn't provide immediate
pleasure, but it may pay on the long run.

61
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:20,760
This holds for traders, mercenaries, workers,
servants, prostitutes, artisans, quacks, assassins,

62
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:26,380
tax investigators and many other kinds of
people. So, human nature uses again the happy-field-trick

63
00:05:26,380 --> 00:05:31,010
to attract people to wealth. This is why pomp
is considered beautiful.

64
00:05:31,010 --> 00:05:34,380
Earthlings often attach little trinkets made
of precious metals and gems to their body

65
00:05:34,380 --> 00:05:39,300
to increase their attractivity. This works
because being wealthy is sexy, but also because

66
00:05:39,300 --> 00:05:44,400
the pomp happyfield around these trinkets
add to the beauty happyfield around the person.

67
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:46,510
Earthlings call these trinkets jewelry.

68
00:05:46,510 --> 00:05:51,480
However, earthling beauty includes more than
landscapes, females and pomp: Beauty can also

69
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:57,140
apply to shapes, patterns or even ideas. This
abstract beauty is determined by criteria

70
00:05:57,140 --> 00:06:03,550
like proportion, symmetry, smooth forms, simplicity,
contrast and self-similarity. But why should

71
00:06:03,550 --> 00:06:07,990
nature tag those things as beautiful?
Some criteria like symmetry and smooth forms

72
00:06:07,990 --> 00:06:12,950
may be inherited from sexual attractivity.
Also, smooth rocks may indicate the presence

73
00:06:12,950 --> 00:06:17,520
of hydric acid during rainy seasons. But I
doubt that this is enough to explain the sense

74
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:19,260
of abstract beauty.

75
00:06:19,260 --> 00:06:24,190
It may have to do with solving abstract problems.
Even complicated problems have often surprisingly

76
00:06:24,190 --> 00:06:28,870
simple and elegant solutions. Bio administrators
often use this when they want to influence

77
00:06:28,870 --> 00:06:33,630
the thought process of some native genius
creature. They scan the brain of the genius,

78
00:06:33,630 --> 00:06:38,390
observe the thought process, and then tag
simple and elegant ideas with tiny happyfields,

79
00:06:38,390 --> 00:06:42,940
because simple and elegant ideas may lead
to a simple and elegant solution.

80
00:06:42,940 --> 00:06:47,110
Abstract beauty works the same way. Consider
a prehistoric earthling who is about to invent

81
00:06:47,110 --> 00:06:52,630
the wheel. That's what he got so far: An irregular,
pentagonal wheel which works, but makes five

82
00:06:52,630 --> 00:06:57,390
"hops" at every turn. Logic may lead the earthling
to think that by cutting off some corners,

83
00:06:57,390 --> 00:07:02,140
he can reduce the number of hops per turn.
But that's the wrong approach. Now, the sense

84
00:07:02,140 --> 00:07:06,850
of beauty may lead him into the opposite direction,
to a more elegant shape : A circle. And as

85
00:07:06,850 --> 00:07:12,460
it turns out, that's actually a pretty good
shape for a wheel. So, when dealing with problems,

86
00:07:12,460 --> 00:07:17,620
beauty may be a hint to a solution. That's
maybe why earthlings say that beauty is "the

87
00:07:17,620 --> 00:07:18,990
splendor of truth."

88
00:07:18,990 --> 00:07:23,260
Scientific advice: When you experiment on
earthlings, you might want to examine the

89
00:07:23,260 --> 00:07:27,850
way their brains process patterns. You will
notice that some patterns are easier to process

90
00:07:27,850 --> 00:07:32,330
than others. Now, there is a theory that the
ease to process patterns is actually connected

91
00:07:32,330 --> 00:07:38,300
to - beauty! Earthlings call this the "processing
fluency theory of aesthetic pleasure".

92
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:42,800
Remember this painting? Now we understand
why earthlings consider it so beautiful: It

93
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:47,630
shows a wealthy, attractive, but not salacious
woman in front of a rather fertile landscape,

94
00:07:47,630 --> 00:07:52,730
surrounded by mountains which provide fresh
hydric acid. Besides, the paintings composition

95
00:07:52,730 --> 00:07:57,360
follows simple geometric rules and is almost
symmetric. And although the painter goes easy

96
00:07:57,360 --> 00:08:01,560
on the pomp, the painting itself is worth
roughly the equivalent of seven million Republic

97
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:04,140
Credits, which certainly adds to the appeal.

98
00:08:04,140 --> 00:08:08,900
Of course, in this case, there is no real
landscape, no real woman, it's all paint on

99
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:13,930
sheets of cellulose, an elaborate deception
of the senses. That's what earthlings call

100
00:08:13,930 --> 00:08:17,360
"art". We will come back to this phenomenon
in a moment.

101
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:20,990
During the last episodes, we have seen that
the Beast manipulates the Ego with different

102
00:08:20,990 --> 00:08:25,730
kinds of pleasures, or, if you want, with
different kinds of happy-fields: The fun-field

103
00:08:25,730 --> 00:08:30,500
around games and stories, the sexy-field around
attractive earthlings, the yummy-field around

104
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:35,169
food, the love-field around family, the cute-field
around cubs, the funny-field which I will

105
00:08:35,169 --> 00:08:40,310
explain in another episode, and the the beauty-field
around things like flowers, jewels and hyperbolic

106
00:08:40,310 --> 00:08:41,519
paraboloids.

107
00:08:41,519 --> 00:08:46,259
As beauty is kind of an all-purpose happyfield,
nature uses it often to amplify sexy-fields,

108
00:08:46,259 --> 00:08:51,930
cute-fields and love-fields. So, earthlings
may find these things beautiful.

109
00:08:51,930 --> 00:08:56,379
Now, earthlings have learned to imitate the
stimuli that generate all these happyfields:

110
00:08:56,379 --> 00:09:02,129
Some drugs imitate fun, porn imitates sexual
stimuli, diet drinks imitate sweetness, stuffed

111
00:09:02,129 --> 00:09:07,750
animals and dolls imitate loved beings, lolcats
imitate small animals, jokes imitate funny

112
00:09:07,750 --> 00:09:11,129
situations, and art imitates the stimuli of
beauty.

113
00:09:11,129 --> 00:09:15,339
The phenomenon of art is similar to what happens
to some administrated planets when the bio-administrator

114
00:09:15,339 --> 00:09:20,839
is gone. Sometimes, the natives find a remaining
happybox, retro-engineer it and build their

115
00:09:20,839 --> 00:09:26,939
own happyboxes. These boxes are then sold,
put onto public places and into showrooms,

116
00:09:26,939 --> 00:09:31,129
where they flood the environment with totally
pointless happywaves. Rich natives wear tiny

117
00:09:31,129 --> 00:09:35,389
happy-boxes around their neck to be more appealing,
or exhibit the boxes in their house to show

118
00:09:35,389 --> 00:09:40,339
their wealth. Individuals who conceive new
happywave patterns become rich and famous,

119
00:09:40,339 --> 00:09:44,310
companies use happy-boxes for advertizing,
and the production of boxes and happywave

120
00:09:44,310 --> 00:09:47,870
patterns becomes a whole new industry.

121
00:09:47,870 --> 00:09:52,490
Exactly the same happens on earth - only without
the happyboxes. Earthlings called artists

122
00:09:52,490 --> 00:09:57,680
have learned to imitate the stimuli of beauty
in paintings, sculptures, and so on. These

123
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:02,819
objects are called artworks. Art is related
to natural beauty like diet drinks are related

124
00:10:02,819 --> 00:10:07,699
to actual sugar, or porn to actual sex: They
imitate the stimuli of pleasure, but out of

125
00:10:07,699 --> 00:10:10,629
context and deprived of their utility.

126
00:10:10,629 --> 00:10:14,790
Not surprisingly, earthling art often focuses
on beautiful people, and on the abundance

127
00:10:14,790 --> 00:10:20,120
of nature - landscapes, flowers, fruits, and
all kinds of living creatures.

128
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:25,560
Except for the microbes.

129
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:31,040
Tips for tourists. If you are interested in
art, visit an art museum. However, you should

130
00:10:31,040 --> 00:10:36,089
avoid modern art, as it often challenges or
distorts the concept of beauty. Better start

131
00:10:36,089 --> 00:10:40,050
with classical art, it's much easier to understand.

132
00:10:40,050 --> 00:10:44,120
Art is not limited to visual stimuli: One
of the most important indicators of fertile

133
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:49,110
regions are bird songs, which are in consequence
considered beautiful. Now, earthlings have

134
00:10:49,110 --> 00:10:54,110
developed something that sounds like an attempt
to imitate bird songs: Music. The most common

135
00:10:54,110 --> 00:10:58,759
methods to make music are singing, blowing
into metal tubes, and using vibrating strings

136
00:10:58,759 --> 00:11:03,170
attached to hollow boxes. The development
of music has probably also been influenced

137
00:11:03,170 --> 00:11:09,259
by prehistoric rituals, sexual selection,
and by imitation of bird songs for hunting.

138
00:11:09,259 --> 00:11:13,050
Earthlings love beauty so much that they even
conceive everyday objects to be all artsy

139
00:11:13,050 --> 00:11:19,730
and beautiful, like clothing, chairs or buildings.
Earthlings call this "design". Like art, design

140
00:11:19,730 --> 00:11:24,600
follows trends - what is beautiful today may
become ugly in some decades.

141
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:29,579
A particularly interesting case of design
are individual vehicles called cars. Regardless

142
00:11:29,579 --> 00:11:36,160
of trends, cars have always a stylized face
on the front. Why is this so? I've no idea.

143
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:41,550
Maybe earthlings are afraid of fast moving
faceless objects, like landslides, forest

144
00:11:41,550 --> 00:11:47,310
fires, killer waves, or swarms of furious
insects. So they put faces onto their cars

145
00:11:47,310 --> 00:11:50,670
to make them less frightening.

146
00:11:50,670 --> 00:11:55,019
Strategic advice. If you want to gain the
earthlings' trust before taking over the planet,

147
00:11:55,019 --> 00:11:58,860
it won't be easy if they think your ships
are ugly. So you might want to abduct some

148
00:11:58,860 --> 00:12:03,569
earthling designers and have them design a
beautiful landing shuttle. Elegant forms,

149
00:12:03,569 --> 00:12:07,449
white paint and a touch of blue or green are
great for convincing earthlings that you "come

150
00:12:07,449 --> 00:12:11,920
in peace". However, you should go easy on
the pomp because A), earthlings associate

151
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:16,860
exaggerated pomp with tyrants and crime lords,
and B), the natives may be tempted to steal

152
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:22,329
your spaceship.

153
00:12:22,329 --> 00:12:27,259
Art may seem like an absurdity, a self-deception,
a global joke. But you can also see it from

154
00:12:27,259 --> 00:12:32,139
another angle: As an attempt of mankind to
grow beyond the necessity of biology. Earthlings

155
00:12:32,139 --> 00:12:36,230
live under the tyranny of the genetic imperative,
much more than they generally realize - but

156
00:12:36,230 --> 00:12:41,040
maybe art, and beauty in general, are a way
of escaping from the grip of this tyrant,

157
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:45,410
of tricking their own nature into giving them
happiness without biological necessity.

158
00:12:45,410 --> 00:12:50,889
On the other hand, you could say the same
about lolcats, diet drinks or porn. So...

159
00:12:50,889 --> 00:12:56,470
Anyway, this was episode 6 of Earthlings 101.
On a personal note, I will be on vacation

160
00:12:56,470 --> 00:13:02,350
next month; I plan to visit the orbital castles
of erioL. So, the next episode will probably

161
00:13:02,350 --> 00:13:07,899
not come before the Galactic Nerdfighter Day,
or, in earthling terms, beginning of September.

162
00:13:07,899 --> 00:13:12,019
In the next episode, we will learn about the
social mechanisms behind words like "hello",

163
00:13:12,019 --> 00:13:17,079
"please", "thank you" and "sorry". We also
learn why international karma trade is big

164
00:13:17,079 --> 00:13:17,980
business.

165
00:13:17,980 --> 00:13:24,980
As always, thanks for watching. And don't
forget to be alien!

